From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 04:29:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 29/30] build: migrate self-hosted TypeScript builds to tsrs

Bundle pinned tsrs with the CLI and remove compiler selection. Resolve the
launcher relative to the SDK, force no emission, preserve file observation
and diagnostic retries, and wait for diagnostic streams before returning.
An empty project must not hide another compiler error. Older tsc-based
clients remain compatible without a backend protocol change.

Check SDK sources and emit public/internal declarations with tsrs. Copy each
declaration tree into the corresponding ESM and CommonJS package layouts
instead of compiling identical declarations twice. Keep runtime bundling and
internal API removal intact, and express non-shared byte-buffer ownership
without copying uploads or imposing generic typed arrays on public types.

Check the Node executor, system UDFs and UDF runtime with tsrs. The backend
bundles original system UDF sources, so drop their unused ES5 output. Watch
runtime tsconfig inputs from Cargo and retain assignment-style class fields.

Migrate supporting ESM/declaration builds and produce their CommonJS output
with esbuild. Check the design system, shared dashboard and self-hosted
Next application with tsrs, including generated route types before Next's
asset build. Preserve aliases, output layouts and actual runtime contracts.
Retain TypeScript where API consumers such as zshy and Next require it.

Document supported hosts and remaining API-based build tooling. Preserve the
global release-age policy and unrelated workspace dependency resolutions.

Keep machine-readable diagnostics unformatted, decode subprocess UTF-8 across
pipe chunks, and check explicit projects without bundling their application.
Limit declaration alias rewriting to source aliases, preserving runtime
React package imports independently of type-resolution overrides.
